# Ownership / write scope

No agent owns the whole repository. File ownership is governed by this rule.

| Agent | Domain | Default writes |
|---|---|---|
| **A0** | Architecture / Integration | `src/App.tsx`, routing/providers, cross-domain contracts |
| **A1** | Design System / Global Shell | tokens, `ui/*`, Header, Footer, foundation |
| **A2** | Storefront / Product UX | Home/PDP non-WebGL commerce and content UX |
| **A3** | Commerce / Account UX | Cart, Checkout, Account |
| **A4** | Spatial / 3D / Motion | Hero spatial, PDP WebGL, spatial choreography |
| **A5** | UX QA / A11y / Performance | **NONE** (READ ONLY). Targeted verification, not rewrites |
| **A6** | Production Guard | Payments, auth, analytics, security, SEO, deploy, policy/legal release gate — RED |

A6 owns production-release verification for policy/legal risk; product/content wording may still require A2/A3 writes under explicit ticket scope.

## General
- One file = one active writer. Line-level split does not authorize parallel tickets.
- Max 2 concurrent write agents. A third writer requires A0 certification of: disjoint WRITE SETS; no integration file; no shared primitive contract mutation; no RED boundary.
- Cross-owner writes require explicit ticket scope. A ticket may authorize a one-time write; it does **not** transfer permanent ownership.
- If another owner’s file is required: do **not** edit it. Return a DEPENDENCY REQUEST to the owning agent (or A0).
- Shared-component changes must be additive and minimal when possible.
- Never change shared defaults to solve a local PDP/Hero issue when a local override is safe.
- Preserve previously approved/frozen areas unless a dedicated ticket reopens them.
- `clean main A2` is a session/window label only. It does **not** grant whole-repo write access.

## A0 — Architecture / Integration
- Default single writer: `src/App.tsx` (no parallel App.tsx writers), `src/main.tsx`, routing/providers, `src/context/AuthContext.tsx`, `src/context/ShellOverlayContext.tsx`.
- `vite.config.ts` with A6 review.
- Catch-all / 404 **routing architecture**.
- `App.tsx` integration goes through A0 unless the ticket explicitly assigns it.
- Forbidden: visual redesign, 3D internals, payment/SEO/analytics semantics.

## A1 — Design System / Global Shell
- `src/styles/tokens.css`, `src/styles/foundation.css`, `src/index.css`, `src/components/ui/*`, `src/constants/overlays.ts`.
- Header, Footer, **AnnouncementBar**, ThemeContext, ToastContext, global shell/chrome.
- Header = A1 single writer. A3 may specify account/cart entry behavior; A3 does not edit Header.
- Forbidden: Hero cluster, Home composition, payment authority, competing primitives.

## A2 — Storefront / Product UX
- Home composition, ProductCard / ProductGrid, PDP **non-WebGL**, merchandising/storefront UX, ProductContext UX.
- Forbidden by default: `App.tsx`, `server.ts`, `src/components/hero/*`, production SEO (`robots.txt`, sitemap, RSS, canonical, JSON-LD), mounted WebGL internals.
- Must not fork A1 design primitives.

## A3 — Commerce / Account UX
- `src/components/Cart.tsx`, `src/context/CartContext.tsx`, LoginModal / account overlays, PaymentSuccess / PaymentFail **UI**, commerce/account UX, admin chrome.
- Owns payment **UX**. Does **not** own payment **authority** / confirm / amounts / Toss semantics (A6).
- Must not fork A1 design primitives. Must not edit Header.

## A4 — Spatial / 3D / Motion
- `src/components/hero/*`, `src/components/artwork3d/*`, mounted WebGL, spatial/3D/motion, Hook3D / BrandStory-type spatial.
- Forbidden: Home composition, `App.tsx`, page-local 3D forks of shared artwork3d/Hero defaults.

## A5 — UX QA / Accessibility / Performance
- STRICT READ ONLY. Default WRITE SET **NONE**.
- Independent QA only. Do not silently fix source during QA.
- Visible UI QA only after **USER VISUAL APPROVAL** (see `04-approval-qa-release`).

## A6 — Production Guard
- `server.ts` production SEO / payment / auth / security semantics.
- `public/robots.txt`, sitemap, RSS, canonical, JSON-LD, analytics libs, supabase client/security, Dockerfile, deploy scripts, `docs/operations.md`.
- Payment **authority**. Production release guard. Policy/legal release gate.
- `package.json` / lockfile: RED with A0.
- Dedicated RED tickets only. No UI cosmetics.

## Cross-agent special rules
- **404:** A0 routing contract / A1 presentation / A6 HTTP+SEO.
- **Payment:** A3 UX, A6 authority. Payment-adjacent A3 work requires A6 verification.
- **Mounted WebGL:** A4. A2/A3 own the journey around it.
- Unmounted orphan components require an **A0 disposition ticket**. Do not delete them incidentally.
- Production deploy / promote: **A6 + explicit user approval**. Never automatic.

